WEBVTT

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:31.114
So, to get right to it...

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:34.784
Layfon, can you use this?

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:40.457
It's a little heavy... Yeah, I think so.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.771
I don't even know what to say!

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:10.987
Are you satisfied?

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:12.739
Huh?

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:18.036
Incidentally, regarding this hair...

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:24.167
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:27.712
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:35.136
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:40.850
<i>Chizu o ushinatte samayotteiru machi</i>

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:44.312
<i>Owariyuku sekai demo</i>

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:51.027
<i>Karada no oku de hashiru</i>
<i>no o yamenai inochi o kikasete</i>

00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:54.322
<i>Tayasanai hikari o tozasanai hitomi ni</i>

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:57.701
<i>Kawaitemo yakitsuketa</i>

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:04.332
<i>Kizutsuku koto mo naku te ni</i>
<i>suru mono nante nanimo shinjinai</i>

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:10.255
<i>Dareka ni mukatta hitosuji no omoi wa</i>

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:18.096
<i>Yoake no you ni hagane no yami o kirisaku</i>

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:22.434
<i>Itsuka brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:26.104
<i>Dakara tsuyoku kaeru</i>

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:32.068
<i>Kasaneta chikara mo inori mo</i>

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:35.739
<i>Kousa suru mirai, kakaeta negai</i>

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:39.159
<i>Dare no te ni mo watasenai</i>

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.702
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:45.707
<i>Kokoro o tsuraneru</i>

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.923
"Adamandite Restored"

00:02:55.342 --> 00:02:57.761
Well, I'm outta here.

00:02:57.761 --> 00:03:01.181
I have to get back to the lab
and go over this data.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.266
What about your classes?

00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:06.227
We don't know when Zuellni
will run into the contaminoids again,

00:03:06.227 --> 00:03:08.063
so it's hardly the time for classes, right?

00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:09.689
About that...

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:19.282
My brother has asked that you
keep this matter in strict confidence.

00:03:19.282 --> 00:03:22.660
I know, I know. See ya!

00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:26.748
Felli, you came here just to pass that along?

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:27.832
Is there a problem?

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:29.459
Uh, no!

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:34.881
Wh-Why?!

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.842
You're overly cooperative, aren't you?

00:03:38.343 --> 00:03:41.179
If you dislike it, why don't you say so?

00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:43.598
There's nothing else that can be done, is there?

00:03:43.598 --> 00:03:46.601
Unless we know more about
the contaminoids, we'll never make it.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.937
But if this goes well,

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:52.565
my brother is sure to make
even more use of you, Fon-Fon.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:57.404
I'm sure. But I don't
think of myself as being used.

00:03:57.404 --> 00:04:02.867
I couldn't stand if someone
died because I didn't do anything.

00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:04.744
That's the extent of it.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.706
Fon-Fon...

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:10.792
You're an idiot, aren't you?

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:13.962
How cruel!

00:04:13.962 --> 00:04:15.714
What an idiot.

00:04:16.131 --> 00:04:19.926
Sure enough, Layfon is fantastic!
This is gonna keep me <i>so </i>busy!

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.553
Yaaay!

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:22.929
Sir!

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.557
'Sup? So you guys stayed out all night too?

00:04:25.557 --> 00:04:28.184
No, I'm, uh, not especially...

00:04:28.184 --> 00:04:30.770
If you are, you should tell me, too.

00:04:31.312 --> 00:04:32.856
I'm sorry!

00:04:32.856 --> 00:04:34.524
I'm in a hurry!

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:36.151
Sheeit.

00:04:37.318 --> 00:04:39.237
And begin sparring!

00:04:53.585 --> 00:04:55.587
Are you all right?

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.965
This is why the third years
don't want to spar with you.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.592
N-No...

00:05:00.884 --> 00:05:02.886
In any case, Lay-ton...

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:06.931
You haven't forgotten I'm a girl, have you?

00:05:10.226 --> 00:05:14.105
True, I already knew they were small,

00:05:14.105 --> 00:05:16.941
but it's still pretty unflattering
when a guy doesn't even notice them.

00:05:16.941 --> 00:05:19.194
No, this was...

00:05:19.194 --> 00:05:21.237
I didn't mean to...

00:05:21.237 --> 00:05:23.239
Uh... sorry.

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.953
I'm just kidding. I know.

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:33.667
Is something wrong with your platoon leader?

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.877
She looks that way to you too, Naruki?

00:05:35.877 --> 00:05:38.296
Actually, about that...

00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:44.761
You saw her going alone somewhere at night?

00:05:44.761 --> 00:05:46.346
Y-Yes.

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:49.557
She's definitely working tonight, correct?

00:05:50.517 --> 00:05:52.143
Yes.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.187
Here it is!

00:05:57.607 --> 00:05:59.776
Just where is she going, I wonder...

00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:02.570
Could that be my scandal sense tingling?!

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.865
Have we uncovered the 17th Platoon
leader's torrid love interest?

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.325
Stop that!

00:06:07.325 --> 00:06:08.451
Why?

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:10.078
Ma'am...

00:06:17.335 --> 00:06:21.548
It doesn't seem like she
just missed her stop, huh?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.027
Restoration.

00:06:52.328 --> 00:06:56.458
<i>I have to get stronger... Stronger!</i>

00:06:56.458 --> 00:06:57.917
Wow...

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.336
I'm impressed.

00:06:59.336 --> 00:07:01.755
Don't tell me every day she's been...

00:07:01.755 --> 00:07:04.549
That's just reckless.
She's pushing herself too hard!

00:07:04.549 --> 00:07:08.595
At this rate, she'll end up hurting herself.

00:07:10.221 --> 00:07:14.934
Sure enough, she's training
apart from her normal classes.

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:18.521
On top of her cleaning duties
at the machinery department, this is...

00:07:18.521 --> 00:07:22.317
Why's she doing this?
Because her platoon lost the last competition?

00:07:22.317 --> 00:07:24.694
That's not the only reason.

00:07:24.694 --> 00:07:28.156
I think I understand, even if only a little.

00:07:28.156 --> 00:07:32.911
The reason, Lay-ton,
is that you're too powerful.

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:38.333
I thought the same thing when
you helped me with my police duties.

00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:42.754
It would be impossible
for me to fight alongside you in battle.

00:07:42.754 --> 00:07:44.964
And that made me feel sad...

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:46.800
as well as frustrated.

00:07:47.342 --> 00:07:50.136
And to be honest, jealous.

00:07:51.388 --> 00:07:53.682
Your leader wants to become stronger.

00:07:53.682 --> 00:07:55.767
As the leader of your platoon...

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:58.269
and moreover, as a fellow military artist.

00:07:58.269 --> 00:08:02.315
It's only natural for a military
artist to want to be stronger.

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:04.943
Military artists always stand alone.

00:08:04.943 --> 00:08:08.947
To become stronger, you must confront yourself.

00:08:10.031 --> 00:08:14.786
But the 17th Platoon is a <i>team</i>, right?

00:08:16.621 --> 00:08:22.252
If you want to get stronger,
why not do it together?

00:08:27.799 --> 00:08:29.426
Ma'am!

00:08:34.014 --> 00:08:38.018
Coming after me wasn't your best decision.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:49.821
Saya! To the left!

00:08:56.578 --> 00:08:59.873
I swear. I never thought
a third-year Military Arts student

00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:04.544
would collapse like some novice.

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.212
Her kei artery has been overworked.

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:07.714
Will she get better?

00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:11.092
I've just strengthened
the kei flow with that needle.

00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:13.720
But she won't be able to move for a while.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.514
Sorry, but please look after her for a bit.

00:09:16.514 --> 00:09:19.851
Don't worry. Once the needle's out,
she'll be like any other patient.

00:09:19.851 --> 00:09:23.355
Y-Yes. Thank you very much.

00:09:24.147 --> 00:09:26.024
Still, good thing huh?

00:09:26.024 --> 00:09:27.942
I swear, Nina's always been like this.

00:09:27.942 --> 00:09:31.237
Once she sets her mind on
something she's blind to everything else.

00:09:33.907 --> 00:09:36.409
I wonder if we can't cover
her with a sheet or something.

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:40.372
Well, the doctor didn't do anything,
so maybe we shouldn't...

00:09:40.789 --> 00:09:42.123
Pervert.

00:09:42.457 --> 00:09:45.126
--Right outta nowhere!
--We weren't looking!

00:09:45.126 --> 00:09:48.004
It's that kind of response
that makes you a pervert.

00:09:48.004 --> 00:09:53.093
In any case... this is what
the probe brought back this morning.

00:09:53.843 --> 00:09:57.514
Zuellni isn't changing its path. At this rate,

00:09:57.514 --> 00:10:00.725
we will probably be discovered
by the contaminoids tomorrow.

00:10:00.725 --> 00:10:05.021
This is bad! I have to hurry
up and finish the adamandite!

00:10:05.021 --> 00:10:08.775
My brother wants you to go out this evening.

00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:10.527
Understood.

00:10:10.527 --> 00:10:13.154
Okay, see you later!

00:10:13.154 --> 00:10:15.782
Will Lay-ton be all right by himself?

00:10:15.782 --> 00:10:17.784
With the platoon leader hospitalized,

00:10:17.784 --> 00:10:19.577
there'll be lots of things he'll need, right?

00:10:19.577 --> 00:10:26.209
We'll take care of that. There's
no way Lay-ton can do it all himself, right?

00:10:38.847 --> 00:10:40.515
Where am I?

00:10:40.515 --> 00:10:44.602
You're already awake? That's just like you.

00:10:45.353 --> 00:10:49.399
Layfon? Oh. I collapsed, didn't I?

00:10:49.399 --> 00:10:52.235
You used too much augmenting kei.

00:10:52.235 --> 00:10:54.612
Have you been watching the whole time?

00:10:54.612 --> 00:10:55.613
No.

00:10:55.905 --> 00:10:57.365
What a screwup this is.

00:10:57.365 --> 00:10:59.868
I don't think so.

00:10:59.868 --> 00:11:01.619
Why not?

00:11:01.619 --> 00:11:04.789
I think there are some things
we can't know unless we almost die.

00:11:04.789 --> 00:11:09.210
It's something that no one can help us with.

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:11.546
And this is the result?

00:11:11.546 --> 00:11:12.922
What a joke.

00:11:12.922 --> 00:11:18.803
At first, I just wanted
to get strong enough to win.

00:11:18.803 --> 00:11:25.018
But then I got a little greedy.
Because... you're so strong.

00:11:25.018 --> 00:11:28.855
The first time I saw how
strong you are, I was afraid.

00:11:28.855 --> 00:11:32.025
I thought, are you even human?

00:11:32.025 --> 00:11:37.530
But when I felt that, sure enough,
you're human, then I got greedy.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:44.162
I thought, unfoundedly,
that the 17th Platoon had gotten stronger.

00:11:45.872 --> 00:11:48.458
But we lost.

00:11:48.458 --> 00:11:50.919
We lost, and I thought
that was actually a good thing...

00:11:50.919 --> 00:11:56.966
Because that competition corrected my mistake.

00:11:56.966 --> 00:12:03.807
But if that's the case, what should I do to win?

00:12:04.849 --> 00:12:08.853
Were you aware
of the disruption in your kei-soku?

00:12:08.853 --> 00:12:14.693
That kind of disruption
means there is too much waste.

00:12:15.068 --> 00:12:17.320
The kei-soku is the foundation of your kei.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.322
Ultimately, we should ideally

00:12:19.322 --> 00:12:22.575
be able to live our daily lives by the kei-soku.

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:24.661
By the kei-soku?

00:12:24.661 --> 00:12:29.666
First, stop thinking of yourself as human.

00:12:29.666 --> 00:12:34.045
I know full well how to fight alone,

00:12:34.045 --> 00:12:37.549
but in terms of group
fighting, I'm practically worthless.

00:12:37.549 --> 00:12:41.803
Please instruct us. Whether we
can become the strongest platoon

00:12:41.803 --> 00:12:47.308
all depends on you.
So... please don't toss us aside.

00:12:47.308 --> 00:12:48.852
Layfon...

00:12:48.852 --> 00:12:53.356
Idiocy. Toss you aside, you say?

00:12:54.441 --> 00:12:56.943
Those sounded just like your last words.

00:12:56.943 --> 00:12:59.237
You were listening?

00:12:59.237 --> 00:13:01.823
I used nen'i to eavesdrop.

00:13:01.823 --> 00:13:04.242
Those weren't my last words.

00:13:04.242 --> 00:13:07.746
Given the situation, it would not
be strange for them to be taken as such.

00:13:07.746 --> 00:13:08.747
I don't know...

00:13:08.747 --> 00:13:10.373
I do.

00:13:11.332 --> 00:13:15.462
Anyway, I don't feel I'm going to lose.

00:13:35.231 --> 00:13:36.858
How is it?

00:13:36.858 --> 00:13:39.986
It's a male, a fourth- or fifth-stager.

00:13:39.986 --> 00:13:42.405
You can tell by how
much the legs have atrophied.

00:13:42.405 --> 00:13:46.743
Contaminoids cast off
their legs every time they molt.

00:13:46.743 --> 00:13:51.373
Anyway, now's my chance,
while he's not moving!

00:14:00.507 --> 00:14:02.342
He was waiting!

00:14:03.134 --> 00:14:05.970
They're hungry after they've molted...

00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:11.893
So he held off molting till
the last minute, when food was near!

00:14:11.893 --> 00:14:13.687
What are you saying?

00:14:13.687 --> 00:14:16.690
What could be my last words!

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:19.818
This is a first-term elder.
Please remember that.

00:14:19.818 --> 00:14:22.028
If you prepare yourself
for half the city being destroyed,

00:14:22.028 --> 00:14:23.655
you may be able to beat it.

00:14:23.655 --> 00:14:25.657
Restoration-02!

00:14:33.623 --> 00:14:35.917
Yo, Nina! You doin' well?

00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:39.129
I don't think that's a question
to ask a sick person.

00:14:39.129 --> 00:14:41.423
You are abso-friggin'-lutely correct.

00:14:41.423 --> 00:14:44.926
Still, collapsing from fatigue, huh?

00:14:44.926 --> 00:14:48.096
You gave us a bit of a surprise,
Miss Platoon Leader.

00:14:48.096 --> 00:14:50.432
I feel badly about that.

00:14:50.432 --> 00:14:55.562
Aw, I don't expect ya
to go apologizin' for it now.

00:14:55.562 --> 00:14:59.315
Anywho, I'm here to talk about somethin' else.

00:14:59.315 --> 00:15:01.151
Something else?

00:15:03.528 --> 00:15:05.530
Sharnid! What are you doing?!

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:08.074
There's no "what" about it.

00:15:08.074 --> 00:15:12.412
You and I are probably
the only ones outta the loop.

00:15:12.412 --> 00:15:17.125
Look Harley, everyone's got things they hide...

00:15:17.125 --> 00:15:21.671
But there's not-so-important stuff
and then there's important stuff.

00:15:21.671 --> 00:15:26.343
What are you doin' with Felli
and the others all secret-like?

00:15:26.343 --> 00:15:29.512
What are you usin' Layfon to have him do?

00:15:29.512 --> 00:15:31.514
That's...

00:15:31.514 --> 00:15:37.187
If possible, I'd like
to hear it from your mouth.

00:16:13.973 --> 00:16:15.975
Restoration-AD!

00:16:29.739 --> 00:16:32.492
I just barely got one wing, huh?

00:16:33.368 --> 00:16:34.577
Fon-Fon?

00:16:34.577 --> 00:16:37.747
Felli! How much time has passed?

00:16:37.747 --> 00:16:41.876
About a day. Zuellni
has changed course during that time.

00:16:41.876 --> 00:16:43.378
It has?

00:16:43.378 --> 00:16:48.049
Didn't you hear? Zuellni
is moving away at considerable speed.

00:16:48.049 --> 00:16:51.302
So hurry up and come back here, Fon-Fon!

00:16:51.302 --> 00:16:53.013
I can't do that.

00:16:53.013 --> 00:16:54.639
But...

00:16:54.639 --> 00:16:57.559
If an elder develops the special ability to fly,

00:16:57.559 --> 00:17:00.687
it would probably be easy
for him to reach Zuellni.

00:17:00.687 --> 00:17:03.314
I have to stop him here!

00:17:04.733 --> 00:17:06.234
Fon-Fon, also--

00:17:06.234 --> 00:17:11.948
Well, how long will it take
to regrow wings? Two days? Three?

00:17:11.948 --> 00:17:14.242
I'll stay on him as long as it takes!

00:17:41.019 --> 00:17:42.812
Layfon!

00:17:42.812 --> 00:17:44.147
Ma'am?

00:17:44.147 --> 00:17:49.819
There's no way we could let
you go off looking cool all by yourself!

00:18:03.416 --> 00:18:04.376
Layfon!

00:18:04.376 --> 00:18:05.835
What are you doing here?

00:18:05.835 --> 00:18:09.214
We're here to pick you up.
You're gonna need a ride back, right?

00:18:09.214 --> 00:18:12.801
Please get out of here! If I defeat him,
a rescue team will come for me.

00:18:12.801 --> 00:18:15.011
<i>Can </i>you defeat him?

00:18:15.387 --> 00:18:17.931
That dite's already at its limit, right?

00:18:17.931 --> 00:18:21.601
Could you really defeat that
contaminoid with a dite like that?

00:18:21.601 --> 00:18:22.977
Just one more blow...

00:18:22.977 --> 00:18:26.856
If I can get one good strike
on the forehead like before...

00:18:27.023 --> 00:18:30.568
All right then. In that case,
I'll increase your chances of winning.

00:18:30.568 --> 00:18:32.404
That thing is hungry.

00:18:32.404 --> 00:18:36.491
If food is in front of it,
it'll make right for it. For sure.

00:18:36.491 --> 00:18:37.534
Ma'am?

00:18:37.534 --> 00:18:40.370
Use that. Use your enemy's actions

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.331
to bring the situation
to your advantage. It's basic.

00:18:43.331 --> 00:18:45.291
You can't mean...?!

00:18:45.291 --> 00:18:49.629
I just hope there's a canyon
close by we can draw him into.

00:18:49.629 --> 00:18:52.924
I can confirm one 20 kilmels ahead.

00:18:52.924 --> 00:18:57.762
Felli?! You can project your nen'i this far?

00:19:01.016 --> 00:19:04.811
The contaminoid has begun moving. Hurry.

00:19:04.811 --> 00:19:08.732
Roger. I will protect your lives.

00:19:08.732 --> 00:19:10.233
Don't talk foolishness.

00:19:10.233 --> 00:19:11.818
I'm platoon leader.

00:19:11.818 --> 00:19:15.530
I'm the one who'll protect your lives.

00:19:16.156 --> 00:19:19.492
Ma'am. Thank you very much.

00:19:43.725 --> 00:19:45.560
You're at the mission point.

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:46.561
Roger.

00:19:46.561 --> 00:19:48.188
Okay!

00:19:51.358 --> 00:19:53.610
When you're ready, ma'am!

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:56.237
<i>Take notice, contaminoid.</i>

00:20:00.784 --> 00:20:04.788
<i>Layfon... Is this the world</i>
<i>you've grown up seeing?</i>

00:20:05.497 --> 00:20:09.626
<i>But from now on, I won't let you go at it alone!</i>

00:20:09.626 --> 00:20:13.463
<i>You have us. We're comrades!</i>

00:20:17.926 --> 00:20:21.262
<i>So let's all fight together!</i>

00:20:33.608 --> 00:20:36.111
<i>Let's get stronger!</i>

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.835
Good work.

00:21:03.388 --> 00:21:05.807
Man, talk about lame.

00:21:05.807 --> 00:21:10.812
We bring that thing down
looking all cool, and <i>this </i>is how it ends?

00:21:10.812 --> 00:21:12.439
Ow!

00:21:13.064 --> 00:21:17.235
In the end, I just got a little off-kilter, huh?

00:21:17.235 --> 00:21:21.072
Thanks to you, we narrowly escaped death.

00:21:21.072 --> 00:21:25.744
This victory belongs to us,
the 17th Platoon. So...

00:21:26.536 --> 00:21:29.664
I hope we can keep counting on you, ma'am.

00:21:30.457 --> 00:21:32.042
Of course!

00:21:32.042 --> 00:21:33.209
Hmm...

00:21:33.209 --> 00:21:34.169
What?!

00:21:34.169 --> 00:21:37.505
Well, it sooorta strikes me

00:21:37.505 --> 00:21:41.760
that maybe, ma'am,
you have a thing for younger guys.

00:21:42.552 --> 00:21:43.887
Where did that come from?

00:21:43.887 --> 00:21:46.723
You're not serious!
He's my subordinate, my comrade!

00:21:46.723 --> 00:21:49.434
Nothing more, nothing less!

00:21:49.934 --> 00:21:51.269
How friggin' boring.

00:21:51.269 --> 00:21:52.812
What's boring?!

00:21:52.812 --> 00:21:56.232
No, nothing at all!

00:22:05.784 --> 00:22:07.410
Hey!

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:14.376
Hey!

00:22:35.313 --> 00:22:38.191
<i>Kioku no hate ni</i>

00:22:38.191 --> 00:22:46.741
<i>Sagashiteita risou no miraizu</i>

00:22:46.741 --> 00:22:57.794
<i>Nanika ga kowakute,</i>
<i>wakaranakute, hitori de furuete</i>

00:22:57.794 --> 00:23:08.930
<i>Anata ga miezu ni itsumo aisou waratte </i>

00:23:08.930 --> 00:23:18.064
<i>Kimi no ude no naka dakareteita</i>

00:23:18.064 --> 00:23:23.737
<i>Samete yuku yo ni koi o shite</i>

00:23:23.737 --> 00:23:29.284
<i>Yume no naka made tsurete itte</i>

00:23:29.284 --> 00:23:34.956
<i>Itsudatte kimi wa, itsudatte kimi wa</i>

00:23:34.956 --> 00:23:43.715
<i>Itsudatte boku ni yasashii uso tsuita</i>

00:23:53.933 --> 00:23:56.519
<i>The leader of the 5th Platoon, Gorneo Lueckens,</i>

00:23:56.519 --> 00:23:59.022
<i>has a reason for which he cannot forgive Layfon.</i>

00:23:59.022 --> 00:24:03.735
<i>But the 5th and 17th Platoons</i>
<i>are ordered on a joint expedition...</i>

00:24:03.735 --> 00:24:06.321
<i>Next time, "A Former Enemy</i>
<i>Reduced to a Ruined City," and...</i>

00:24:06.321 --> 00:24:08.128
<i>Restoration!</i>
